# Allowlist for bin/design-tokens.
#
# Format: <path> | <one-line reason>
#   - A path ending in "/" is a directory prefix (every file under it).
#   - Any other path is an exact file match.
#
# Every entry needs a reason that still holds; an entry whose reason has
# expired (the file no longer does what it says) should be deleted, not kept
# "just in case".
#
# Prefer an exact file to a directory, because a directory entry also exempts
# every file added to it later, under a reason that may not apply to them.
# `lib/config/` was measured and rejected on exactly that ground: only
# `wind_theme.g.dart` is generated, and the other thirteen files in that
# directory are hand-authored, so the directory form would have exempted them
# under a reason that is false for all of them. `lib/app/mocks/` stays a
# directory because its reason ("fixture data, never rendered as real UI") does
# hold for every file in it, present and future. Neither `lib/resources/` nor
# `lib/resources/views/` is listed: only the one file under it that actually
# carries the operator palette.

lib/config/wind_theme.g.dart | generated by design:sync from DESIGN.md; not hand-authored
lib/app/mocks/ | fixture data for previews/tests, never rendered as real UI
lib/app/models/status_page.dart | domain fallback color when an operator's stored hex is malformed
lib/resources/views/status/status_form_support.dart | kBrandColors is the operator-chosen brand palette; content, not a semantic design token
lib/app/support/brand_contrast.dart | the two on-colour extremes DESIGN.md already names, needed as values because the choice is computed against an operator's colour rather than written as a className
